{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1424726276,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc1NjM1NTE1","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/44#issuecomment-75635515"},"message":"actually workaround for testing would be to clone that submodule into another temp directory -- then annex works properly","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1424883541,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc2MDAxNjU0","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/44#issuecomment-76001654"},"message":"http://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/Git_annexed_files_symlink_are_wrong_when_submodule_is_not_in_the_same_path/\n\nDue to the way git submodules work, if you intend to use a git-annex\nrepository as a submodule, you can _only_ use it as a submodule, and it\nhas to always be located in the same place relative to its parent\nmodule.\n\nI do not see a way around this. (Other than using direct mode.)\n\n## \n\nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1424884608,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc2MDA3MDY5","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/44#issuecomment-76007069"},"message":"ah right -- just stoke me that indeed if repository is initialized as an existing submodule (not added anew) its .git is just a file containing a pointer to \"upstairs\" .git/ directory ... lame :-/  And the only way around this was if annex was not hidden under .git/annex but rather was an independent directory in the root of the repository (e.g. as .annex). \n\nSo is important to keep it in mind as a limitation of git-annex then (existing independent annex'ed repos can't be used as submodules), heh heh","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1424884623,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI0MTg2NjEzMw=="},"added":["wontfix"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1424884701,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc2MDA3NzMw","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/44#issuecomment-76007730"},"message":"@joeyh but how much git-annex relies on hardcoded .git/annex path? ;)  i.e. may be some time there could be an option to initialize it outside of the .git/? ;)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1424887940,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc2MDIwODc4","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/44#issuecomment-76020878"},"message":"Even though I have marked it as 'wontfix' for now: I have initiated a new milestone ([Git-annex: big refactoring 1](https://github.com/datalad/datalad/milestones/Git-annex:%20big%20refactoring%201)) where we could collate those issues we identified, you agree that they are worth tackling, but it would require a massive refactoring of annex code/structure.  For now I have placed there #32 since you are already dealing with it somewhat, and it might be worth moving this #44 there?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1424896794,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc2MDUxMzg1","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/44#issuecomment-76051385"},"message":"Yaroslav Halchenko wrote:\n\n\u003e ah right -- just stoke me that indeed if repository is initialized as an\n\u003e existing submodule (not added anew) its .git is just a file containing a\n\u003e pointer to \"upstairs\" .git/ directory ... lame :-/\n\nIt might work to replace the \"gitlink\" file with a symlink.\n\n## \n\nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1424919566,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc2MTEzOTUx","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/44#issuecomment-76113951"},"message":"replacing .git with a symlink sounds like begging for a trouble ;)  but I could be proven wrong (that git folks envisioned this crippled .git file as a cross-platform symlink replacement and otherwise test proper git functioning whenever .git is a symlink to somewhere high up ;))","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1424923218,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc2MTE4NjA1","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/44#issuecomment-76118605"},"message":"BTW -- in #40 we were considering submodules to mitigate large collections... with  #44  I guess it wouldn't be the best option really since would disallow  dealing with a particular subset of annexes","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1425068461,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc2NDY0ODE5","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/44#issuecomment-76464819"},"message":"(My email reply was rejected by github for some reason. Repost.)\n\n\u003e replacing .git with a symlink sounds like begging for a trouble ;)\n\nI tried it, and it seems to work ok, at least for the limited number of\nthings I know to do with submodules. Note that after converting .git to\na symlink, I had to edit .git/config and remove the core.worktree\nsetting.\n\nSee:\nhttp://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/Git_annexed_files_symlink_are_wrong_when_su\nbmodule_is_not_in_the_same_path/#comment-8eeb2ec8891cf95e9d4e7623000299e4\n\n\u003e BTW -- in #40 we were considering submodules to mitigate large collections...\n\u003e with #44 I guess it wouldn't be the best option really since would disallow\n\u003e dealing with a particular subset of annexes\n\nIt would be ok using the above approach, a submodule then uses the same\nsymlink paths as does a regular repository.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f9